[Applause]  chair of the executive committee of  nickel Awards fellows Eric  welcome everyone to the 2022 Nickel  fellowships in screenwriting Awards and  live read  my name is Eric heiserer I'm a member of  the writers branch of the Academy of  Motion Picture Arts and Sciences and  chair of the nickel committee  Tonight We Gather for an incredible  story told on Hallowed Ground the land  of the tongfa people its original  caretakers  we honor tongfa ancestors and the Tango  Community today which continues to  nurture this land and water through  traditional practices activism art and  education  we also honor indigenous communities  around the world the early storytellers  which brings me to our purpose tonight  to nurture Empower and celebrate an  inclusive community of storytellers of  writers this is the nickel fellowship's  Mission first launched in 1986 by an  amazing woman Gladys G Nichol a mission  informed by G's career as an actor and  writer and inspired by the life of her  beloved writer producer husband Don  nickel  cut to 2022 and G's Vision has become  kind of a success  since its Inception 37 years ago the  nickel competition has received over 188  000 entries  and only 176 fellowships have been  awarded  as such being named Nico fellow is a big  deal  here's some more numbers this year alone  the competition received  5526 scripts from an astounding 84  different countries  these stories and all their stages of  development and success were judged by  83 professional readers including  graduates of the Academy's diverse  reader training Workshop then 178  Academy members winnowed down those  scripts through more rounds of judging  in the end my incomparable Fellowship  committee colleagues and I chose the  Nichols newest fellows six in all  authors of five exemplary screenplays  tonight we'll meet these new fellows  we'll witness their winning screenplays  brought to life  but for me beyond the competition  process it's Global reach it's 35 000  prize it's mentorship opportunities the  evolution of Gene Nichols vision is  about the Deep connections made between  the tinkle fellows  I'm a writer first and foremost so the  power of the nickel story is about  advocating for this special community of  writers not only across the year-long  fellowship but in the years that come  after  now due to the pandemic we were unable  to celebrate the 2021 fellows in person  last year please join me in welcoming to  the stage our 2021 nickel fellows Haley  hope artels  Karen delapena Collison  Byron Hamel  RJ Daniel Hannah  and Laura Kosen  I know there's a lot of hard work that  led to winning the fellowship  maybe you still remember getting that  call from the nickel committee  together with a 21-2021 fellows we are  very excited to share the story of six  extraordinary screenwriters tonight and  here's the moment they became the newest  members of our nickel family  [Music]

